 "title": "Director of Equalization (Assessor's Office) - Welcome to Day County, South Dakota!",
 "text": "Director of Equalization (Assessor's Office) - Welcome to Day County, South Dakota!\nOctober 18, 2026\nWelcome to Day County, South Dakota!\nHome\nDirectory »\nAmbulance\nAuditor’s Office\nClerk of Courts\nCommunity Health Nurse / WIC Office\nDirector of Equalization (Assessor’s Office)\nDriver’s License\nEmergency Management Office\nExtension Office\nHighway Department\nPlanning & Zoning Office\nRegister of Deeds’ Office\nSheriff’s Office\nState’s Attorney\nTreasurer’s Office\nVeterans Service Office\nWeed & Pest\nWelfare Office\nCommission »\nCommission Agenda\nCommission Minutes\nElections\nEmployment\nCities/Towns\nTownship\nAlerts\nCounty GIS\nYou are here: Home / Director of Equalization (Assessor’s Office)\nDirector of Equalization (Assessor’s Office)\nHOURS: 8:00am – 5:00pm Monday-Friday\nBarbra Block, Director\n711 W. 1 st Street, Suite 203\nWebster, SD 57274\n(605) 345-9502\nFax (605) 345-9503\ndoe@day.sdcounty.gov\nStephanie Williams, Clerk\nDAY COUNTY GIS\nCounty Directors of Equalization are appointed to their office by the Board of County Commissioners. Their responsibility is to assess all real property in the county for property tax purpose. By law, the assessed value must be its full and true or market value. Resident persons dissatisfied with their assessment may appeal to the local board, the county board, the Office of Hearing Examiners (OHE) and then the courts. Consequently, an appeal may not be made to the county board of equalization without a previous appeal having been made to the local board, and so on. Non-resident property owners first step in the appeal process would be to the county board of equalization.\nEqualization\nApril 14, 2026 Minutes\nReturn to top of page\nCopyright © 2026 on Genesis Framework · WordPress · Log in",
